{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]Caleb Meyer he lived alone, In them hollerin [G]pines
[G]And he made a little whiskey [D]for himself said it helped to pass the [Am]time
[Am]Long one evening in back of my house, Caleb come [G]around
[G]And he called my name till [D]I went out, With no-one else [Am]around
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]Caleb Meyer your ghost is gonna wear them rattling [G]chains
[G]But when I go to [D]sleep at night, Don't you call my [Am]name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Am]Where's your husband Nellie Cane, Wheres your darlin' [G]gone?
[G]Did he go on down the [D]mountainside, and leave you all [Am]alone?
[Am]Yes my husband's gone to Bowling Green, to do some business [G]there
[G]Then Caleb threw that [D]bottle down, And grabbed me by my [Am]hair
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
